1
00:00:09,542 --> 00:00:10,977
Why are you running away?

2
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,479
Mr. Nao!

3
00:00:13,013 --> 00:00:14,981
"This isn't a normal part-time job.

4
00:00:15,648 --> 00:00:17,350
I'm probably doing something wrong."

5
00:00:17,417 --> 00:00:18,284
I MUST KEEP DOING THE JOB

6
00:00:20,153 --> 00:00:21,888
"Whatever it takes.

7
00:00:23,990 --> 00:00:25,458
I will protect her."

8
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,493
I WILL PROTECT HER

9
00:00:38,405 --> 00:00:39,539
What are you thinking?

10
00:00:42,108 --> 00:00:44,244
When and where did you get this?

11
00:00:45,245 --> 00:00:48,014
This morning, Chika gave it to me.

12
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:49,949
It's Tabatake's notebook, right?

13
00:00:50,016 --> 00:00:53,820
Maybe. Chika said she didn't know.

14
00:00:53,887 --> 00:00:55,455
Neither she nor I have read it yet.

15
00:00:55,522 --> 00:00:59,192
You threw it away because you learned
what was written in it, didn't you?

16
00:00:59,993 --> 00:01:03,496
It had information that would jeopardize
Tabatake's life insurance claim.

17
00:01:03,563 --> 00:01:05,165
So you threw it in the river.

18
00:01:05,231 --> 00:01:06,399
I didn't throw it. I dropped it.

19
00:01:06,466 --> 00:01:08,234
-You threw it!
-I dropped it.

20
00:01:13,306 --> 00:01:16,176
Thanks to you, I can't read it at all.

21
00:01:18,278 --> 00:01:19,345
I see.

22
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:22,582
I wanted to read it too.

23
00:01:22,649 --> 00:01:24,918
Cut it out. You're pissing me off.

24
00:01:26,286 --> 00:01:30,523
Did it say how Tabatake
was involved in the crime?

25
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:31,558
I don't know.

26
00:01:31,624 --> 00:01:33,426
The reason Tabatake died?

27
00:01:33,493 --> 00:01:35,195
-I don't know.
-This thing…

28
00:01:35,261 --> 00:01:36,529
Did you make a copy?

29
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:40,166
I'm really busy today.
Someone even broke into my place.

30
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:42,635
Did you do that yourself? You faked it.

31
00:01:42,702 --> 00:01:44,037
Surely it wasn't you, Ogoma?

32
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,338
Of course not.

33
00:01:45,405 --> 00:01:47,540
What about other officers?

34
00:01:47,607 --> 00:01:49,409
That scary-looking one?

35
00:01:50,243 --> 00:01:51,544
He looks like he could…

36
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:54,781
The police don't use illegal means.
We would be fired.

37
00:01:54,848 --> 00:01:56,950
They say you cover for your own.
Cover up scandals.

38
00:01:57,016 --> 00:01:59,252
That doesn't happen anymore.

39
00:02:06,693 --> 00:02:09,062
The drug Ms. Tabatake was carrying

40
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:11,731
is circulating again.

41
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,501
Ms. Tabatake carried the raw ingredient.
She didn't carry CAN-d.

42
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:16,269
It's the same thing!

43
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,742
What the Narcotics officer said

44
00:02:24,811 --> 00:02:26,546
is happening now.

45
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:31,184
Lives and futures will be ruined.
That must not happen.

46
00:02:36,723 --> 00:02:37,824
Mr. Nao.

47
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:47,367
Tell me everything that was written in it.

48
00:02:51,704 --> 00:02:53,606
I haven't read it, so I don't know.

49
00:02:57,911 --> 00:03:00,947
I'll submit it to the police as evidence.
I'll tell Chika myself…

50
00:03:01,014 --> 00:03:03,082
You will do nothing!

51
00:03:04,817 --> 00:03:05,919
I'll do it.

52
00:03:10,490 --> 00:03:12,592
The family hasn't read it?
Neither has Nao?

53
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:15,895
I called Ms. Tabatake's sister…

54
00:03:15,962 --> 00:03:17,830
I haven't read it.

55
00:03:18,698 --> 00:03:21,768
You handed it to Mr. Nao
without reading it?

56
00:03:24,671 --> 00:03:26,873
Mr. Nao hasn't read it either.

57
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,374
Mr. Nao too?

58
00:03:28,441 --> 00:03:31,945
Hey, which sauce goes with this?

59
00:03:32,679 --> 00:03:35,715
Sorry. I really haven't read it.

60
00:03:36,616 --> 00:03:37,584
That notebook--

61
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:43,423
Let's try submitting it to Forensics.
Long shot, though.

62
00:03:43,489 --> 00:03:44,624
Excuse me.

63
00:03:44,691 --> 00:03:46,092
Thank you.

64
00:03:48,361 --> 00:03:50,563
What is Nao trying to do?

65
00:03:51,364 --> 00:03:54,968
He's trying to prove
Tabatake's death wasn't a suicide.

66
00:03:56,502 --> 00:03:59,939
If it's suicide, the daughter
won't get the life insurance,

67
00:04:00,506 --> 00:04:03,977
and without money, she won't survive.

68
00:04:10,817 --> 00:04:12,986
I heard from the Shikara Police Station.

69
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,356
About my sister's notebook.

70
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:20,760
Sorry for not telling you.
I had to submit it to them.

71
00:04:20,827 --> 00:04:22,829
In the process, it got wet.

72
00:04:23,830 --> 00:04:25,298
But I have taken photos…

73
00:04:26,466 --> 00:04:29,102
of every page of the notebook.

74
00:04:29,669 --> 00:04:32,272
As you and Nono said,

75
00:04:32,839 --> 00:04:36,876
your sister was being threatened
and was struggling because of it.

76
00:04:37,543 --> 00:04:43,316
She was given a job by a man named Tsugaru
and was roped into some trouble.

77
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:45,451
Um…

78
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,122
this job…

79
00:04:50,556 --> 00:04:53,993
Was it a normal job?

80
00:04:57,497 --> 00:04:59,732
From this notebook,

81
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:03,569
I can only tell she was asked
to deliver something.

82
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:08,574
Do you have anything else
your sister left behind?

83
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:13,346
No, only the bankbook
and the insurance policy.

84
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:17,684
What is happening
with your sister's apartment?

85
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:22,689
COLCHICINE POISONING

86
00:05:22,755 --> 00:05:23,623
Poison…

87
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:27,360
A break-in… The notebook…

88
00:05:27,427 --> 00:05:30,797
CAN-d… A courier…

89
00:05:31,597 --> 00:05:33,866
A mastermind…

90
00:05:36,602 --> 00:05:37,303
MS. AYA

91
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:39,539
Are you free tonight?

92
00:05:40,440 --> 00:05:42,709
I also need to ask you something.

93
00:05:42,775 --> 00:05:44,577
I'll come to you.

94
00:05:47,313 --> 00:05:49,582
Thanks for waiting.

95
00:05:49,649 --> 00:05:51,250
Thank you.

96
00:05:52,118 --> 00:05:54,020
-Welcome.
-Hello.

97
00:06:00,026 --> 00:06:01,427
-Ogoma.
-Huh?

98
00:06:01,494 --> 00:06:02,528
Hey.

99
00:06:05,365 --> 00:06:07,233
Where's Ms. Aya?

100
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,836
She said she'll be late. Have a seat.

101
00:06:10,503 --> 00:06:12,004
Thanks.

102
00:06:12,071 --> 00:06:13,172
Cheers.

103
00:06:13,239 --> 00:06:14,307
Cheers.

104
00:06:18,277 --> 00:06:20,546
When Aya went missing, how did you feel?

105
00:06:20,613 --> 00:06:23,683
I only wanted to save her.
She helped me a lot long ago.

106
00:06:28,621 --> 00:06:30,256
Were you classmates with Ms. Aya?

107
00:06:30,323 --> 00:06:32,024
Yes, from high school.

108
00:06:32,091 --> 00:06:33,559
Aya likes to play the hero,

109
00:06:33,626 --> 00:06:36,462
so every few years,
she gets pulled into some trouble.

110
00:06:36,996 --> 00:06:38,531
Ms. Aya…

111
00:06:39,232 --> 00:06:40,833
Make her happy.

112
00:06:42,335 --> 00:06:43,336
Please.

113
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,338
Who are you to her to ask me that?

114
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:47,440
We're not like that.

115
00:06:48,141 --> 00:06:50,109
There's nothing between Aya and me.

116
00:06:50,643 --> 00:06:54,647
We go out, and I give advice,
but we're not dating.

117
00:06:55,782 --> 00:06:58,551
You must know one or two women like that.

118
00:06:58,618 --> 00:06:59,952
I don't.

119
00:07:00,953 --> 00:07:02,221
All-boys school?

120
00:07:02,288 --> 00:07:03,656
Co-ed.

121
00:07:04,657 --> 00:07:06,826
-Do you have a girlfriend?
-Not now.

122
00:07:07,527 --> 00:07:08,995
Then go for Aya.

123
00:07:13,266 --> 00:07:15,001
I owe her, that's all.

124
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,169
You don't dislike her?

125
00:07:16,235 --> 00:07:18,538
-No.
-Then that means you like her.

126
00:07:18,604 --> 00:07:20,973
I hope Ms. Aya comes soon!

127
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:22,041
You're so loud.

128
00:07:25,178 --> 00:07:26,078
Huh?

129
00:07:26,646 --> 00:07:28,648
Sorry, I probably won't make it.

130
00:07:28,714 --> 00:07:31,417
Whoa, this is the worst.

131
00:07:31,484 --> 00:07:33,319
Let's drink, okay?

132
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,426
This is the worst?

133
00:07:40,493 --> 00:07:41,928
All right, it sucks--

134
00:07:46,165 --> 00:07:50,069
If you feel unwell,
we'll go straight back to the hospital.

135
00:07:51,137 --> 00:07:51,971
Yeah.

136
00:07:53,439 --> 00:07:55,675
Don't try to be strong.
Be sure to tell me.

137
00:07:55,741 --> 00:07:59,345
What is happening
with your sister's apartment?

138
00:07:59,412 --> 00:08:01,647
I thought about it a lot,

139
00:08:04,217 --> 00:08:06,419
and I've decided to let it go.

140
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:10,022
I've explained the situation to Nono.

141
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:14,627
Will Nono go to a children's home?

142
00:08:14,694 --> 00:08:18,130
That's the only option right now.

143
00:08:18,197 --> 00:08:19,565
You'll get tired.

144
00:08:19,632 --> 00:08:24,770
She's scheduled to enter the home
early next week.

145
00:08:26,439 --> 00:08:29,775
Before she does,
once she gets permission to go out,

146
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:33,412
could you take her back to her home
so she can get what she needs?

147
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:38,017
I'm home!

148
00:08:38,584 --> 00:08:40,520
Excuse me.

149
00:08:51,731 --> 00:08:53,566
MATERNAL AND CHILD HEALTH HANDBOOK

150
00:08:54,800 --> 00:08:56,068
-Come here!
-Huh?

151
00:08:56,135 --> 00:08:57,537
Get this for me.

152
00:09:03,009 --> 00:09:03,976
Okay.

153
00:09:06,479 --> 00:09:08,881
I'm little, so it's easy!

154
00:09:20,760 --> 00:09:23,729
I knew I couldn't live here anymore.

155
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:28,601
The counselor
said the same thing as you, mister.

156
00:09:28,668 --> 00:09:31,671
Children can't live alone.

157
00:09:33,506 --> 00:09:38,878
It's silly how adults
all say the same things.

158
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,381
It is what it is.

159
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:44,884
I have to give up.

160
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,854
You give up fast.

161
00:09:50,289 --> 00:09:52,224
You don't need to make so many boxes.

162
00:09:52,291 --> 00:09:53,259
Why?

163
00:09:53,993 --> 00:09:56,862
I'm only allowed to bring one box.

164
00:09:57,530 --> 00:10:01,267
Where I'm going,
there are lots of children,

165
00:10:01,334 --> 00:10:03,836
so I can't bring a lot of things.

166
00:10:04,971 --> 00:10:06,272
Then…

167
00:10:07,707 --> 00:10:10,242
the most important things go in this box.

168
00:10:10,309 --> 00:10:12,678
This box will go with you
to the new place.

169
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:16,616
The next most important things
go in this other box.

170
00:10:17,917 --> 00:10:20,820
If that's not enough,
I'll make more boxes.

171
00:10:20,886 --> 00:10:23,422
And I'll keep them.

172
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,491
Can I put Mommy's things in too?

173
00:10:25,558 --> 00:10:26,659
Of course.

174
00:10:32,298 --> 00:10:33,666
Take your time.

175
00:10:33,733 --> 00:10:34,767
Okay.

176
00:10:49,382 --> 00:10:52,818
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

177
00:10:53,819 --> 00:10:55,454
-Ogoma.
-Yes?

178
00:10:55,988 --> 00:10:57,857
Hurry up and eat. It will get cold.

179
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:00,426
Thanks for the meal.

180
00:11:05,731 --> 00:11:06,732
Ogoma.

181
00:11:07,266 --> 00:11:08,434
Ogoma.

182
00:11:08,501 --> 00:11:09,869
The deputy chief wants to see you.

183
00:11:09,935 --> 00:11:11,737
Did you do something again?

184
00:11:12,371 --> 00:11:13,205
No.

185
00:11:13,739 --> 00:11:14,874
Hurry up.

186
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,409
Excuse me.

187
00:11:22,882 --> 00:11:23,983
Sit.

188
00:11:24,550 --> 00:11:25,384
Yes.

189
00:11:29,555 --> 00:11:30,823
Excuse me.

190
00:11:33,826 --> 00:11:37,229
When you took leave
and investigated in Tokyo…

191
00:11:37,296 --> 00:11:38,964
I'm sorry!

192
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:41,233
Hear us out first.

193
00:11:43,335 --> 00:11:47,940
You heard about the drug case
from the joint team, right?

194
00:11:48,774 --> 00:11:49,608
Yes.

195
00:11:49,675 --> 00:11:51,911
They're expanding their investigation.

196
00:11:51,977 --> 00:11:55,114
Our station is to send one person.

197
00:11:56,749 --> 00:12:00,019
Teruyuki Nikaido is an important witness.

198
00:12:01,287 --> 00:12:03,723
HQ says to send someone
who's worked on the case from the start.

199
00:12:03,789 --> 00:12:04,724
What?

200
00:12:05,925 --> 00:12:08,928
I'm going? Not Mr. Awashima?

201
00:12:10,062 --> 00:12:13,032
You'll provide our station's information
to the joint team.

202
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:15,434
A kind of liaison.

203
00:12:15,501 --> 00:12:18,404
The mission is serious!
You're going alone.

204
00:12:19,038 --> 00:12:20,139
Yes.

205
00:12:20,206 --> 00:12:22,274
Tomorrow, the 16th, 8:00 a.m.

206
00:12:22,341 --> 00:12:24,844
Attend the joint meeting at Kitami HQ.

207
00:12:24,910 --> 00:12:25,745
Don't be late!

208
00:12:26,979 --> 00:12:29,115
I'll do it! I'll give it my all!

209
00:12:29,181 --> 00:12:30,583
All right!

210
00:12:33,552 --> 00:12:35,788
-See you tomorrow.
-See you.

211
00:12:35,855 --> 00:12:38,224
-Bye.
-See you tomorrow.

212
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:44,830
KITAUCHI MIDDLE SCHOOL
BADMINTON CLUB

213
00:13:03,549 --> 00:13:05,417
Sorry I couldn't go yesterday.

214
00:13:05,484 --> 00:13:08,988
It's fine, I drank a lot with Mr. Nobori.

215
00:13:09,054 --> 00:13:10,756
Wasn't he annoying?

216
00:13:10,823 --> 00:13:12,992
He can be kind of weirdly friendly.

217
00:13:13,058 --> 00:13:15,928
No, I hadn't had that much fun in a while.

218
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:20,065
I heard about your high school days.

219
00:13:20,933 --> 00:13:23,202
You don't need to hear that.

220
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:29,809
I met the Narcotics officer
you introduced me to.

221
00:13:31,110 --> 00:13:32,645
They said they'll be careful,

222
00:13:33,512 --> 00:13:36,649
so as not to alarm the students.

223
00:13:36,715 --> 00:13:39,218
I'm glad I consulted you, Ogoma.

224
00:13:39,285 --> 00:13:40,553
That's great to hear.

225
00:13:42,354 --> 00:13:43,756
Oh, Ms. Aya.

226
00:13:45,291 --> 00:13:47,827
I want to ask what I couldn't yesterday.

227
00:14:09,882 --> 00:14:12,885
What a beautiful place.

228
00:14:12,952 --> 00:14:14,119
Isn't it?

229
00:14:14,653 --> 00:14:17,223
But when I'm here alone,
I'm afraid of bears.

230
00:14:17,289 --> 00:14:19,291
Bears are scary with two people too.

231
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:23,996
Did something good happen?

232
00:14:26,332 --> 00:14:27,299
Yes.

233
00:14:28,133 --> 00:14:29,001
At work.

234
00:14:29,068 --> 00:14:30,836
I see.

235
00:14:30,903 --> 00:14:32,137
They recognized your skills.

236
00:14:32,204 --> 00:14:35,641
I went unrecognized all these years.
It was about time.

237
00:14:37,109 --> 00:14:38,010
Good for you.

238
00:14:40,179 --> 00:14:41,247
Thank you.

239
00:14:44,316 --> 00:14:47,786
I'll probably go to Kitami
more often for work.

240
00:14:47,853 --> 00:14:48,954
I see.

241
00:14:49,855 --> 00:14:53,692
Kitami is nice.
There's a Don Quijote and McDonald's.

242
00:14:53,759 --> 00:14:55,728
I live there too.

243
00:14:55,794 --> 00:14:57,696
Let's go eat next time, for real.

244
00:14:59,498 --> 00:15:00,699
Can it be just the two of us?

245
00:15:01,267 --> 00:15:02,134
Sure.

246
00:15:05,070 --> 00:15:07,306
Nobori is a friend, you know.

247
00:15:08,073 --> 00:15:10,476
Oh, yes. I heard.

248
00:15:10,542 --> 00:15:13,212
I confessed my feelings to him
at our high school graduation,

249
00:15:14,013 --> 00:15:15,347
and he turned me down flat.

250
00:15:15,414 --> 00:15:16,782
He preferred we stay friends.

251
00:15:17,449 --> 00:15:19,518
Now we're just good friends.

252
00:15:21,186 --> 00:15:23,522
Yes, I understand.

253
00:15:25,691 --> 00:15:26,825
Friends.

254
00:15:29,228 --> 00:15:33,632
MOMMY'S IMPORTANT THINGS
PRECIOUS THINGS

255
00:15:36,635 --> 00:15:38,437
Hello. What is it?

256
00:15:40,439 --> 00:15:43,442
I wanted to hear your voice.

257
00:15:45,477 --> 00:15:47,913
Don't be silent. Say something.

258
00:15:49,081 --> 00:15:50,716
What do you want?

259
00:15:53,552 --> 00:15:57,089
It's about the life insurance
I'm investigating.

260
00:15:57,156 --> 00:15:58,757
I want your opinion.

261
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:01,327
Give me your honest opinion,
as an insurance worker.

262
00:16:01,393 --> 00:16:03,429
If it doesn't meet
the contract conditions,

263
00:16:03,495 --> 00:16:05,431
it can't be paid.

264
00:16:06,398 --> 00:16:08,901
Why do you assume it doesn't meet them?

265
00:16:09,435 --> 00:16:12,671
The fact that you're asking me
means it's a difficult case. Right?

266
00:16:16,375 --> 00:16:17,209
Exactly.

267
00:16:17,743 --> 00:16:21,146
The insurance money comes
from our many policyholders' funds.

268
00:16:21,213 --> 00:16:23,282
It is money they entrusted us with.

269
00:16:23,349 --> 00:16:25,584
We can't just pay willy-nilly.

270
00:16:25,651 --> 00:16:27,886
I know. But listen.

271
00:16:27,953 --> 00:16:32,291
The recipient is an eight-year-old girl
with an incurable disease.

272
00:16:32,358 --> 00:16:36,528
If her mother's insurance pays,
it will keep her alive for a while.

273
00:16:39,298 --> 00:16:42,134
Are you trying to force a payout?

274
00:16:43,235 --> 00:16:45,070
How much is it?

275
00:16:45,604 --> 00:16:46,705
30 million yen.

276
00:16:47,773 --> 00:16:50,642
Can you tell me
how far you're willing to force it?

277
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,582
If you can't tell me,

278
00:16:57,483 --> 00:16:58,817
you shouldn't do it.

279
00:17:03,088 --> 00:17:07,026
Maybe so.

280
00:17:07,092 --> 00:17:09,862
I'm done. I put everything in the boxes.

281
00:17:12,164 --> 00:17:13,866
Hey, just now…

282
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:22,808
MOMMY'S IMPORTANT THINGS

283
00:17:22,875 --> 00:17:24,009
All good.

284
00:17:46,331 --> 00:17:47,433
Let's go.

285
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:48,967
Yeah.

286
00:17:57,242 --> 00:17:58,377
Wow!

287
00:17:58,444 --> 00:18:01,146
-Amazing!
-So many colors.

288
00:18:04,883 --> 00:18:07,719
Huh? Where is Dr. Yoshino today?

289
00:18:08,353 --> 00:18:09,822
He's on summer vacation.

290
00:18:12,724 --> 00:18:14,393
Wow!

291
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,561
It's amazing.

292
00:18:17,196 --> 00:18:20,332
I want to travel too.

293
00:18:23,569 --> 00:18:25,003
Where do you want to go?

294
00:18:26,004 --> 00:18:27,973
I wonder…

295
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,142
Wow!

296
00:18:44,189 --> 00:18:45,491
Hey.

297
00:18:48,060 --> 00:18:51,897
About the money your mom left for you.

298
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:57,803
Could you wait a bit longer?

299
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:00,906
Will it take time?

300
00:19:02,774 --> 00:19:04,576
A little.

301
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:09,481
I'll wait.

302
00:19:12,618 --> 00:19:14,119
You can take your time.

303
00:20:04,303 --> 00:20:05,437
By the way,

304
00:20:06,071 --> 00:20:08,440
you said there was something
you wanted to know?

305
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:09,575
Right.

306
00:20:11,109 --> 00:20:13,412
Do you know colchicine?

307
00:20:14,146 --> 00:20:16,315
Did someone eat it by mistake?

308
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:18,951
No, someone got it mixed into a drink.

309
00:20:20,185 --> 00:20:22,120
That's too malicious.

310
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:25,557
How would someone put it in a drink?

311
00:20:26,491 --> 00:20:31,230
If it's from a plant,
you can make a liquid with ethanol.

312
00:20:31,296 --> 00:20:33,298
Does that need expert knowledge?

313
00:20:33,365 --> 00:20:36,034
But with the medical colchicine…

314
00:20:36,702 --> 00:20:37,803
Medical?

315
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:41,139
Colchicine is also a drug
used to treat gout.

316
00:20:41,206 --> 00:20:43,575
Crush it, dissolve it, concentrate it…

317
00:20:43,642 --> 00:20:45,410
And you can mix it into a drink.

318
00:20:45,477 --> 00:20:47,079
The culprit is either

319
00:20:47,145 --> 00:20:50,916
a patient prescribed colchicine,
a family member of one,

320
00:20:51,483 --> 00:20:52,718
or a medical worker.

321
00:21:01,226 --> 00:21:02,728
It's all connected, right?

322
00:21:03,729 --> 00:21:05,764
Everything since the mountain accident.

323
00:21:05,831 --> 00:21:08,667
Go to Kitami tomorrow
and get solid information.

324
00:21:09,901 --> 00:21:11,036
-Yes.
-Don't oversleep.

325
00:21:20,746 --> 00:21:24,349
Did you find out who broke into my place?

326
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:26,785
What was stolen?

327
00:21:26,852 --> 00:21:28,720
Nothing valuable.

328
00:21:28,787 --> 00:21:31,490
The target wasn't valuables, was it?

329
00:21:32,224 --> 00:21:35,360
They broke in to steal case materials.

330
00:21:35,427 --> 00:21:38,630
Ms. Tabatake's notebook, I think.

331
00:21:40,232 --> 00:21:41,667
CLIENT: TSUGARU?

332
00:21:41,733 --> 00:21:43,168
I MUST KEEP DOING THE TSUGARU JOB

333
00:21:43,235 --> 00:21:44,670
I WILL PROTECT HER

334
00:21:45,871 --> 00:21:47,939
Who broke in?

335
00:21:49,541 --> 00:21:52,477
In all probability,
a person related to this case.

336
00:21:53,245 --> 00:21:56,114
If you know that much,
please cooperate with the investigation.

337
00:22:00,886 --> 00:22:02,087
Hurry and…

338
00:22:02,854 --> 00:22:04,690
catch the burglar.

339
00:22:05,657 --> 00:22:08,460
I'm scared at night.
I haven't been sleeping well.

340
00:22:32,584 --> 00:22:33,985
Oh, Ms. Aya.

341
00:22:37,289 --> 00:22:38,623
ANONYMOUS NUMBER

342
00:22:44,062 --> 00:22:44,896
Hello?

343
00:22:45,931 --> 00:22:47,132
Ms. Aya?

344
00:22:48,500 --> 00:22:50,001
-What's wrong?
-Ogoma.

345
00:22:50,836 --> 00:22:51,937
It's Yoshino.

346
00:22:54,272 --> 00:22:55,674
Dr. Yoshino?

347
00:23:01,613 --> 00:23:04,182
Where are you?

348
00:23:05,917 --> 00:23:07,953
I have a favor to ask.

349
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:11,123
I'll go to you. Tell me where.

350
00:23:11,957 --> 00:23:13,725
Please look outside your door.

351
00:23:14,393 --> 00:23:16,094
Your apartment's front door.

352
00:23:27,506 --> 00:23:28,840
What is this?

353
00:23:38,683 --> 00:23:39,518
Yes.

354
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:40,419
It's Yoshino.

355
00:23:40,485 --> 00:23:41,887
What do you want?

356
00:23:42,654 --> 00:23:44,089
Please turn the camera on.

357
00:23:46,158 --> 00:23:47,025
The camera?

358
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,527
ANONYMOUS NUMBER

359
00:23:51,997 --> 00:23:57,068
Send me all the investigation data
on Teruyuki Nikaido.

360
00:23:57,636 --> 00:23:59,971
Dr. Yoshino, are you okay?

361
00:24:00,906 --> 00:24:02,674
Is someone threatening you?

362
00:24:02,741 --> 00:24:03,708
No.

363
00:24:04,743 --> 00:24:07,045
I'm the one threatening you.

364
00:24:18,390 --> 00:24:19,991
What is this?

365
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:29,835
Ms. Aya?

366
00:24:36,074 --> 00:24:36,975
MS. AYA

367
00:24:43,415 --> 00:24:46,284
Don't hang up, and follow my instructions.

368
00:24:47,552 --> 00:24:51,256
The hostage will be released once
I receive the investigation materials.

369
00:24:52,424 --> 00:24:56,628
Dr. Yoshino, may I speak with the hostage?

370
00:24:56,695 --> 00:24:57,762
She's asleep.

371
00:24:58,363 --> 00:25:00,332
She won't wake for a while.

372
00:25:01,533 --> 00:25:03,668
Take your hand off your own phone.

373
00:25:09,908 --> 00:25:12,177
Start moving now.

374
00:25:13,111 --> 00:25:14,546
The deadline is 9:00 a.m.

375
00:25:15,046 --> 00:25:20,252
If you tell the police or a third party,
you know what happens to the hostage.

376
00:25:20,819 --> 00:25:24,122
Human life is precious. Act accordingly.

377
00:25:27,125 --> 00:25:30,896
Put in your earphones and put
your phone in your breast pocket.

378
00:25:30,962 --> 00:25:32,564
Hello.

379
00:25:33,431 --> 00:25:35,534
Why are you here at this hour?

380
00:25:36,501 --> 00:25:39,704
I forgot something. Is anyone here?

381
00:25:39,771 --> 00:25:41,506
Probably not.

382
00:25:41,573 --> 00:25:42,407
Thank you.

383
00:25:54,886 --> 00:25:57,856
Take photos of everything
and send me the data.

384
00:25:57,923 --> 00:25:59,224
MT. SHIKARA MURDER CASE

385
00:26:10,869 --> 00:26:12,337
I can't do it.

386
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:13,805
Do you give up?

387
00:26:14,773 --> 00:26:19,878
I'm sorry that Ms. Saruwatari
was suspected of murder.

388
00:26:22,781 --> 00:26:24,316
I imagine you suffered too.

389
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:27,619
Seeing her like that.

390
00:26:33,558 --> 00:26:35,493
Who said anything about giving up?

391
00:26:42,734 --> 00:26:45,036
Can I hand it over in person?

392
00:26:45,837 --> 00:26:48,373
I want to know the hostage is safe.

393
00:26:48,440 --> 00:26:50,542
An exchange. Files for the hostage.

394
00:26:51,476 --> 00:26:52,811
Very well.

395
00:26:53,878 --> 00:26:55,680
Please be on time.

396
00:26:57,482 --> 00:26:58,149
Yes.

397
00:26:59,751 --> 00:27:01,686
TOKORO POLICE STATION

398
00:27:01,753 --> 00:27:04,189
JOINT DRUG INVESTIGATION

399
00:27:09,427 --> 00:27:11,463
Officer Ogoma isn't here yet.

400
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:12,497
Huh?

401
00:27:14,265 --> 00:27:16,568
Hey, Ogoma! Ogoma?

402
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:18,036
Hey! We're coming in!

403
00:27:18,103 --> 00:27:19,838
Ogoma!

404
00:27:22,641 --> 00:27:25,477
Did he get into an accident somewhere?

405
00:27:26,177 --> 00:27:27,112
Huh?

406
00:27:32,217 --> 00:27:34,185
He left all his stuff here.

407
00:27:34,919 --> 00:27:36,855
He left his phone at home?

408
00:27:36,921 --> 00:27:38,990
-This guy is too sloppy!
-What is he doing?

409
00:27:39,057 --> 00:27:40,825
He didn't forget it.

410
00:27:41,559 --> 00:27:44,129
For whatever reason, he left it behind.

411
00:27:44,195 --> 00:27:45,830
What's wrong with Ogoma?

412
00:27:45,897 --> 00:27:47,032
We're talking about that!

413
00:27:47,098 --> 00:27:49,567
He messed up the evidence room, right?

414
00:27:49,634 --> 00:27:50,669
What are you talking about?

415
00:27:50,735 --> 00:27:52,237
It was around 5:00 a.m.

416
00:27:52,303 --> 00:27:53,338
Why is he here?

417
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:55,807
He said he forgot something.

418
00:27:55,874 --> 00:27:57,008
Look here.

419
00:27:57,742 --> 00:27:59,310
The investigation materials?

420
00:27:59,377 --> 00:28:01,946
He's taking photos.

421
00:28:02,013 --> 00:28:03,548
He's going to take them out?

422
00:28:03,615 --> 00:28:05,316
I'll stop the video. Look here.

423
00:28:06,651 --> 00:28:08,486
Whose evidence is this?

424
00:28:08,553 --> 00:28:09,821
Nikaido's?

425
00:28:10,388 --> 00:28:11,623
He took something! What?

426
00:28:13,591 --> 00:28:14,659
He put it in his pocket.

427
00:28:14,726 --> 00:28:16,094
What is he doing?

428
00:28:16,161 --> 00:28:19,664
Deputy chief, we need you
to make a decision now.

429
00:28:19,731 --> 00:28:21,633
Go after Ogoma.

430
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,768
Yoshino is very likely involved.

431
00:28:23,835 --> 00:28:26,638
Yoshino said he went on house calls
once or twice a week,

432
00:28:26,705 --> 00:28:27,872
but 20% are made up.

433
00:28:27,939 --> 00:28:31,976
The day before the hiking tour and
the day of it, he made two false claims.

434
00:28:32,677 --> 00:28:35,213
I have the investigation files.

435
00:28:37,282 --> 00:28:41,286
Honestly, I'm sick of this detective job.

436
00:28:41,352 --> 00:28:45,590
Early mornings, late nights,
no promotion even if you work hard,

437
00:28:45,657 --> 00:28:46,991
poison in your coffee.

438
00:28:48,359 --> 00:28:50,061
Are you listening, Dr. Yoshino?

439
00:28:50,562 --> 00:28:52,630
Can you wake the hostage soon?

440
00:28:53,765 --> 00:28:56,134
If I could hear her voice,
my motivation would go up.

441
00:28:57,569 --> 00:28:58,803
You'll see her soon.

442
00:28:59,838 --> 00:29:01,072
Are you being followed?

443
00:29:03,508 --> 00:29:05,210
Not so far.

444
00:29:10,615 --> 00:29:13,384
Let’s find them from the call records
and the business card.

445
00:29:13,451 --> 00:29:16,588
-Shouldn’t we wait for the deputy chief?
-There’s no time!

446
00:29:16,654 --> 00:29:18,890
His car is gone, but his phone is here.

447
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:21,025
Good morning!

448
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,794
Oh! Hey!

449
00:29:23,695 --> 00:29:25,764
Did you meet Ogoma last night?

450
00:29:25,830 --> 00:29:27,799
I only passed him.

451
00:29:27,866 --> 00:29:29,267
-And Yoshino?
-Huh?

452
00:29:29,801 --> 00:29:30,635
No formalities?

453
00:29:30,702 --> 00:29:33,338
-Did something happen?
-I’m asking if you met Yoshino.

454
00:29:33,404 --> 00:29:35,006
Not in the last three days.

455
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:36,541
Do you know him?

456
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,443
Huh? One moment.

457
00:29:38,510 --> 00:29:39,878
Don’t mess with me.

458
00:29:40,912 --> 00:29:43,248
No clue. Who’s this person?

459
00:29:45,950 --> 00:29:48,086
I ask, but no answers.

460
00:29:49,220 --> 00:29:51,756
Dr. Yoshino is on summer vacation.

461
00:29:52,757 --> 00:29:55,860
He's probably taking it easy.

462
00:29:55,927 --> 00:29:57,262
Do you know where he is?

463
00:29:58,029 --> 00:29:58,963
What?

464
00:29:59,898 --> 00:30:00,965
Hey.

465
00:30:02,734 --> 00:30:03,935
Do you want to know?

466
00:30:04,002 --> 00:30:04,903
Where is he?!

467
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:32,664
Hello?

468
00:30:32,730 --> 00:30:35,366
This is Awashima
of Shikara Police Station.

469
00:30:37,068 --> 00:30:38,169
Police?

470
00:30:38,670 --> 00:30:40,538
Chief, it's from Mr. Awashima.

471
00:30:40,605 --> 00:30:42,307
He found Yoshino’s current location.

472
00:30:42,373 --> 00:30:43,374
How?

473
00:30:44,409 --> 00:30:45,577
This is Inoue!

474
00:30:45,643 --> 00:30:48,213
Nao planted a GPS tag on Yoshino.

475
00:30:50,281 --> 00:30:54,018
Was he really going on house calls?

476
00:31:34,659 --> 00:31:36,828
Take the left path.

477
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:37,762
Yes.

478
00:31:37,829 --> 00:31:39,764
NO ENTRY

479
00:31:45,003 --> 00:31:47,605
Can you see a building with a round roof?

480
00:32:04,956 --> 00:32:06,724
Dr. Yoshino.

481
00:32:07,625 --> 00:32:08,693
Mr. Ogoma.

482
00:32:13,231 --> 00:32:14,565
Good work.

483
00:32:18,569 --> 00:32:19,671
Sit down.

484
00:32:41,025 --> 00:32:41,726
Here.

485
00:32:42,593 --> 00:32:44,128
Thank you.

486
00:32:52,437 --> 00:32:53,304
Hey.

487
00:32:54,038 --> 00:32:54,906
Is Ms. Aya…

488
00:32:54,973 --> 00:32:56,341
First, the goods.

489
00:32:58,009 --> 00:32:59,344
She's safe, right?

490
00:33:25,403 --> 00:33:26,471
I’ll check them.

491
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:33,745
LOADING

492
00:33:38,216 --> 00:33:39,250
Can you see the data?

493
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,087
Don’t rush me.

494
00:33:44,622 --> 00:33:45,690
Have a drink.

495
00:33:52,263 --> 00:33:55,333
I told you to follow
my instructions, didn’t I?

496
00:34:01,506 --> 00:34:02,573
Sure.

497
00:34:08,913 --> 00:34:09,814
Over there.

498
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:11,883
Hey!

499
00:34:11,949 --> 00:34:13,084
You stay here.

500
00:34:14,118 --> 00:34:15,119
Yes.

501
00:34:16,687 --> 00:34:18,623
NO ENTRY

502
00:34:28,499 --> 00:34:29,534
Chief,

503
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:32,904
this is what Ogoma
took out of the evidence cabinet.

504
00:34:32,970 --> 00:34:34,272
An SD card?

505
00:34:34,338 --> 00:34:37,575
It's an illegal device that swipes
your data once connected to a PC!

506
00:34:38,676 --> 00:34:40,545
LOADING

507
00:34:48,886 --> 00:34:49,887
Who is this?

508
00:34:49,954 --> 00:34:52,290
Mr. Ishibashi and his grandchild.

509
00:35:00,131 --> 00:35:02,800
Deceiving people isn’t good. I mean it!

510
00:35:03,401 --> 00:35:04,936
Do you not care about the hostage…

511
00:35:21,586 --> 00:35:22,553
Don't move!

512
00:35:53,684 --> 00:35:54,652
Ogoma.

513
00:35:57,221 --> 00:35:58,222
Ogoma?

514
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:00,758
Yoshino…

515
00:36:05,630 --> 00:36:07,431
Hey! Ogoma!

516
00:36:08,299 --> 00:36:09,734
What happened…

517
00:36:09,800 --> 00:36:11,769
-Mr. Nao.
-Whoa! Are you okay?

518
00:36:11,836 --> 00:36:12,770
He got me.

519
00:36:13,404 --> 00:36:16,040
Don't move. We have to stop the bleeding.

520
00:36:17,475 --> 00:36:19,243
Yoshino got away.

521
00:36:19,310 --> 00:36:20,678
Okay.

522
00:36:21,913 --> 00:36:23,748
Don't move!

523
00:36:24,682 --> 00:36:25,917
There.

524
00:36:28,786 --> 00:36:30,354
Move your hand.

525
00:36:31,389 --> 00:36:32,690
Okay.

526
00:36:39,864 --> 00:36:40,998
-You okay?
-Yes.

527
00:36:41,065 --> 00:36:42,967
It hurts!

528
00:36:44,135 --> 00:36:45,403
I'm back!

529
00:36:45,469 --> 00:36:47,104
What happened? Ogoma!

530
00:36:47,171 --> 00:36:49,373
-I’m totally fine.
-Are you okay?

531
00:36:57,315 --> 00:36:58,583
Ms. Aya.

532
00:36:59,684 --> 00:37:00,818
What?

533
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:03,888
Your leg…

534
00:37:03,955 --> 00:37:05,489
I'm fine.

535
00:37:05,556 --> 00:37:06,991
Are you okay, miss?

536
00:37:08,926 --> 00:37:12,496
I was kidnapped, supposedly.

537
00:37:13,264 --> 00:37:15,333
You actually weren’t, right?

538
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:17,401
Yeah.

539
00:37:22,006 --> 00:37:24,875
What happened?

540
00:37:29,213 --> 00:37:30,381
Yesterday,

541
00:37:31,816 --> 00:37:34,518
on my way home, my car stalled.

542
00:37:36,454 --> 00:37:37,588
What's wrong?

543
00:37:37,655 --> 00:37:39,991
A passerby helped me,

544
00:37:40,625 --> 00:37:43,561
but my phone was stolen then.

545
00:37:44,695 --> 00:37:47,999
Your car’s coolant had been drained.
It was planned.

546
00:37:50,368 --> 00:37:51,802
Who did it?

547
00:37:54,238 --> 00:37:55,273
Don't know.

548
00:37:55,339 --> 00:37:58,042
You should stay away
from your home for a while.

549
00:37:58,109 --> 00:38:00,978
There’s a place to stay
at my company. Use it.

550
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:03,047
Okay.

551
00:38:05,650 --> 00:38:06,751
Sorry.

552
00:38:09,754 --> 00:38:10,721
And…

553
00:38:11,922 --> 00:38:12,757
Mr. Nobori.

554
00:38:14,091 --> 00:38:16,027
-Thank you very much.
-It's nothing.

555
00:38:21,532 --> 00:38:22,900
You really are a detective.

556
00:38:23,868 --> 00:38:26,570
I told you many times, he is!

557
00:38:26,637 --> 00:38:29,340
CRIMINAL INVESTIGATIONS

558
00:38:53,998 --> 00:38:54,865
Are you okay?

559
00:38:56,100 --> 00:38:57,168
Yes.

560
00:38:58,969 --> 00:39:00,438
How many stitches?

561
00:39:01,272 --> 00:39:03,007
I'll get over it
with a good night's sleep.

562
00:39:04,942 --> 00:39:06,410
Thank you.

563
00:39:07,411 --> 00:39:08,512
Your job?

564
00:39:09,113 --> 00:39:10,581
Did you get fired?

565
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:12,917
They are questioning me tomorrow.

566
00:39:15,886 --> 00:39:16,954
There you go.

567
00:39:24,161 --> 00:39:27,131
You came all the way
to Lake Anuma to help me.

568
00:39:27,698 --> 00:39:29,767
Looked like a hostage situation, you know.

569
00:39:29,834 --> 00:39:31,969
Yoshino was lying.

570
00:39:33,270 --> 00:39:35,639
It's the same with fraud calls,

571
00:39:35,706 --> 00:39:39,143
if the person doesn’t answer the phone,
it’s 99% a lie.

572
00:39:39,210 --> 00:39:41,645
But on the 1% chance, it was real…

573
00:39:42,413 --> 00:39:44,382
Ms. Aya would have been in danger.

574
00:39:46,016 --> 00:39:47,318
You called Mr. Nobori too,

575
00:39:48,152 --> 00:39:49,787
didn't you?

576
00:39:50,454 --> 00:39:52,456
The police did most of the work.

577
00:39:52,523 --> 00:39:53,624
Thanks for the food.

578
00:39:54,625 --> 00:39:55,893
That man…

579
00:39:56,560 --> 00:40:01,432
He contacted lots of people
and found Ms. Aya.

580
00:40:04,235 --> 00:40:07,338
Coming! What's wrong, Nobori?

581
00:40:07,405 --> 00:40:08,406
Aya, is she here?

582
00:40:08,472 --> 00:40:10,174
She is. But what?

583
00:40:11,342 --> 00:40:13,244
I'm glad! Come with me!

584
00:40:13,310 --> 00:40:14,879
-Why?
-Just hurry!

585
00:40:14,945 --> 00:40:16,147
Nobori!

586
00:40:17,648 --> 00:40:18,816
What happened?

587
00:40:31,295 --> 00:40:32,296
Ogoma!

588
00:40:32,363 --> 00:40:33,564
Ogoma!

589
00:40:34,064 --> 00:40:36,033
Ogoma!

590
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:39,069
He let me know she was safe.

591
00:40:46,877 --> 00:40:49,680
I’ll never be able to repay him.

592
00:40:52,516 --> 00:40:53,851
The police

593
00:40:54,652 --> 00:40:57,588
seemed to have noticed
your intentions too.

594
00:40:58,622 --> 00:41:00,090
They’re good colleagues.

595
00:41:00,758 --> 00:41:04,295
They helped me out so much,
so why did I let Yoshino get away?

596
00:41:25,983 --> 00:41:26,917
What’s this?

597
00:41:30,988 --> 00:41:33,858
A copy of Ms. Tabatake’s notebook.

598
00:41:33,924 --> 00:41:35,693
Every page.

599
00:41:38,128 --> 00:41:40,831
So you did make a copy!

600
00:41:40,898 --> 00:41:44,668
I wanted to find the truth
before the police did.

601
00:41:46,070 --> 00:41:47,238
Really?

602
00:41:47,304 --> 00:41:48,539
I'm telling the truth.

603
00:41:51,108 --> 00:41:52,710
What does it say?

604
00:41:57,014 --> 00:41:58,516
It proves Ms. Tabatake

605
00:41:59,950 --> 00:42:01,952
was being threatened.

606
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:04,421
On the other hand?

607
00:42:06,857 --> 00:42:09,193
It also proves she was involved in crime.

608
00:42:14,632 --> 00:42:16,400
From my standpoint,

609
00:42:17,101 --> 00:42:20,337
that notebook is a double-edged sword.

610
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:26,544
You don't want more people to die
because of this drug.

611
00:42:26,610 --> 00:42:28,512
I understand that.

612
00:42:36,186 --> 00:42:37,321
Use this notebook

613
00:42:40,324 --> 00:42:41,959
for the investigation.

614
00:42:52,236 --> 00:42:53,237
Mr. Nao.

615
00:42:55,506 --> 00:42:58,475
Solving the case isn't all I want,
you know.

616
00:43:00,511 --> 00:43:02,947
I’ll absolutely keep my promise to Nono.

617
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:08,686
I haven’t given up either.

618
00:43:15,225 --> 00:43:16,760
May I read it?

619
00:43:16,827 --> 00:43:17,962
Of course.

620
00:43:20,698 --> 00:43:22,433
Thank you.

621
00:43:50,995 --> 00:43:53,931
Hurry to Doto General Hospital!

622
00:43:53,998 --> 00:43:54,898
Don't die!

623
00:43:54,965 --> 00:43:56,467
It's huge!

624
00:43:56,533 --> 00:43:58,702
Don't forget,
more people will fall victim to it!

625
00:43:58,769 --> 00:43:59,603
Yes!

626
00:43:59,670 --> 00:44:00,638
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
